      <description>Prime Minister Andy Burnham says he wants Britain to reindustrialize and has held out the prospect of rejoining the European Union as an element in that revival. His government needs to pay more attention to chemicals. It’s a sector that offers both a textbook case of the damage wrought by Brexit and a persuasive example of why attempting the long and messy process of reversing the decision would be unwelcome for many businesses.</description>
